From 14cc694a68375692de23ba9e3e1c60245d3d05d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D. Manresa" <dmanresa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:13:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v2 2/2] ipa: ipu3: Add a Sharpness algorithm

The Image Enhancement Filter Directed (IEFD) block of the ImgU combines
denoising with directional and unsharp-mask sharpening. It is the
sharpening block that the ImgU firmware binaries actually run: none of
them enables the Y_EE_NR edge enhancement accelerator, so programming that
block has no effect. When IEFD is not programmed the driver enables it with
a moderate default sharpening, and there is currently no way to change it.

Add a Sharpness algorithm that programs the IEFD block with the driver
defaults and scales the sharpening parameters (unsharp mask amount,
directional sharpening weight and overshoot limits) by a sharpness
factor: 1.0 keeps the driver behaviour, 0.0 disables the sharpening while
keeping the denoising, and values up to 9.0 (where the unsharp mask amount
saturates) sharpen more. The default comes from the optional 'sharpness'
tuning parameter and can be changed at runtime with the Sharpness
control, which is also reported in the metadata.

Enable the algorithm in the uncalibrated tuning file; with the default
value the output is unchanged.

Measured on a Dell Latitude 7275 (OV5670, 1280x720 NV12, same scene): the
standard deviation of the Laplacian of Y is 2.24, 2.47, 2.81 and 3.43 for
sharpness 0.0, 1.0, 4.0 and 9.0, with the mean luminance and chroma
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: D. Manresa <dmanresa@gmail.com>
